## Q1
The SessionStart repair does not follow a symlink or junction and does not run git. `is_real_dir` / `is_real_file` (`crates/c3/src/setup/repo_models.rs:200`) use `symlink_metadata`; on Rust 1.97 `is_dir` / `is_file` are false for a symlink and for a junction reported as one. A `read_dir` name cannot contain `..`. One frontmatter line is replaced; CRLF and a BOM stay (`repo_models.rs:72`). A non-Claude pin, `inherit`, and an alias are not rewritten. `AGENTS.md` changes only to a same-prefix, same-suffix successor (`repo_models.rs:104`).

`C3_CHILD=1` is set in `scrub_host_markers` (`crates/c3/src/engines/mod.rs:54`). `run_turn` calls it after `env_clear` (`subprocess.rs:616`). Maintain's `Env::run` and the codex `--version` probe do too. `hook_line` returns before any edit when that variable is set (`repo_models.rs:251`, `branches.rs:744`). Gaps: `claude_auth::probe` (`claude_auth.rs:96`) clears the environment and never sets `C3_CHILD` (`auth status`, `--version` do not start a session). Detached `c3 maintain` (`maintain/mod.rs:1750`) inherits the parent and does not set it; engine children it starts still go through the scrub. Whether Claude forwards the variable to its own subagents is unproven. `c3 doctor --fix` (`cli/doctor.rs:88`) calls `refresh_repo_models` with no child check, so a reviewer or worker that runs it rewrites the tree. The hook always returns 0 (`hook/mod.rs:2713`). It does not run `git status` or `git cherry`. Those git calls have no timeout.

## Q2
A foreign description that does not start with `c3: ` survives `--set` and `--clear` (`branches.rs:132`, `863`). A failed `git config --get` is treated as empty, so `--set` overwrites (`branches.rs:833`). A note whose first line starts with `c3: ` is removed by `--clear` even when it does not parse. The key is `branch.<name>.description` for the branch `branch_exists` checked; arguments are argv.

The listing and doctor are not read-only. Both run `git status --porcelain` (`branches.rs:542`, `cli/branches.rs:52`, `doctor.rs:279`), which refreshes the index and can take `index.lock`. The hook uses `ScanOpts::default()`. `c3 finish` uses `dirty: false` and only prints a note (`cli/finish.rs:87`); it does not refuse.

Unknown means not ancestry-merged and no record (`branches.rs:339`). Content-merged is display-only, so doctor still counts those branches. Detached worktrees are always unrecorded. With no upstream, behind is counted against the local default. The default branch is `origin/HEAD`, else `main`, else `master`, else HEAD (`branches.rs:197`), so a `develop` repo with `main` present and no `origin/HEAD` is classified against `main`. A directory named `c3-kimi-wt-*` is omitted even when it is the user's (`branches.rs:592`). `git cherry` runs once per unmerged branch, and only for `c3 branches`, not the hook.

## Q3
The catalog GET sends no key and no caller headers (`web.rs:190`). The client adds `User-Agent: c3/<version>` only (`env.rs:174`). Redirects are manual, https, same host, at most 3 hops, plus the existing `code.kimi.ai` to `cdn.kimi.ai` pair (`env.rs:259`), which also applies to a catalog URL on that host. The read stops at 8 MiB (`env.rs:213`); `web.rs` then drops a body over 4 MiB. Ids must pass `valid_model_id` before they are stored, printed, or spliced into roster JSON (`models.rs:564`). Smoke passes `--model` as one argv (`smoke.rs:283`). A hostile body cannot break JSON, a shell, or a path. It can lie about `created` (Q4). Endpoint fetches are a separate call with redirects off.

## Q4
Undated catalog ids and page ids never enter the smoke list (`models.rs:311`). Protected and on-request entries are not smoked (`maintain/mod.rs:1281`, checked again at `1325`). `--dry-run` returns before smoke and `apply_swap`, and neither pass writes state (`mod.rs:776`, `806`). `--models` does not assign `next_due` or the engine records. A major bump is seated only after a smoke on that entry's plan.

Two holes: the entry's own `grok` / `agy` / `endpoint:` ids are candidates with no date check (`models.rs:372`), so a higher number the catalog would reject is smoked if that list contains it. `created` is taken from the catalog body (`models.rs:320`); a later stamp on an older same-family id passes the gate, and a smoke that only checks that the plan answered will seat it.

## Q5
`published_from` keeps `web:` and `page:` sources only, lowercased, full id and vendor-stripped (`models.rs:519`). An `endpoint:` list is not in that set. Telemetry lowercases and strips one trailing `[1m]` (`classes.rs:320`). A private name is sent when that string is in the set, or, for class `anthropic`, when it matches the published Claude shape even if it is not in the closed list (`classes.rs:344`). A private `base_url` on any other host stays `other` unless the published set collides. `model_declared` only widens the effort map (`orchestrate/mod.rs:2424`); it does not change the telemetry token.

## Q6
The walk uses `symlink_metadata`, unlinks `is_symlink()` entries, and does not descend (`kimi.rs:233`). A Windows directory link uses `remove_dir` (`kimi.rs:258`). The root is not unlinked. The test covers a successful unlink only. `remove()` still runs `git worktree remove --force` and `remove_dir_all` when unlink removes nothing (`kimi.rs:215`). A link the walk misses, or a link `remove_link` cannot delete, is left for those two. This review did not prove Git refuses to follow a remaining junction.

## Q7
Not exercised: a real roster swap, a `model_pages` fetch, an `AGENTS.md` rewrite across a major, `--set` on a foreign description, a junction `.claude`, `doctor --fix` under `C3_CHILD=1`, the index refresh, unlink failure then `worktree remove`, Claude subagent inheritance of `C3_CHILD`, and `git cherry` on a large history. CI for `ba43ff6` was still running when the brief was written. Not read in full: CHANGELOG prose, README, templates, and the test bodies past the production paths above.

## Requested checks
RC1. In a scratch repo, run `c3 doctor` and `c3 branches` (no `--set`). Working directory: that repo. Permission: workspace-write. Observation: `.git/index` mtime changes or `index.lock` appears. Budget: 2 minutes. Confirms finding #1.
RC2. Run `grok models`. Permission: read-only. Observation: whether `grok-4.20` is listed beside `grok-4.7`. Budget: one command. Confirms the trigger of finding #2.
RC3. On Windows, a temp worktree with a junction held open so unlink fails, then the kimi `remove` path. Permission: workspace-write. Observation: whether `outside/sentinel.txt` survives. Budget: one test. Confirms finding #5.

### Findings

- **F04-1** [minor] `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:542`, `crates/c3/src/cli/branches.rs:52`, `crates/c3/src/setup/doctor.rs:279` - The c3 branches listing and c3 doctor, both described as read-only, run git status --porcelain in the primary worktree. Git refreshes the index and can create index.lock unless optional locks are disabled. The hook and c3 finish do not run status. Trigger: c3 branches with no --set/--clear, or c3 doctor, in a repository whose index stat cache is stale or whose index is locked by another git process. Evidence: read-code: The listing scan sets ScanOpts { content: true, dirty: true }.; read-code: dirty runs git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no with -C set to the primary worktree path. No --no-optional-locks.; read-code: doctor::scan calls quick_scan(repo_root, true), so the same status runs.; inferred: status updates the index stat cache and takes index.lock unless GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 or --no-optional-locks is set. That flag is not passed. Verify: In a scratch repo, compare .git/index mtime before and after c3 doctor and c3 branches. Remedy: Pass --no-optional-locks (or GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0) on every status, cherry, and rev-list used by the listing, doctor, hook, and finish.
- **F04-2** [major] `crates/c3/src/maintain/models.rs:372`, `crates/c3/src/maintain/mod.rs:1346` - Successors taken from the entry's own grok, agy, or endpoint model list skip the catalog date gate. A numerically higher id that is an older product (grok-4.20 versus grok-4.7) is smoked and, if the plan still answers, seated. Trigger: The engine or endpoint list contains both the seated id and an older same-prefix same-suffix id with a higher version, and C3_MAINTAIN_MODELS swaps. Evidence: read-code: own ids are copied into cands unconditionally. public_verdict filters only the public ids in others.; read-code: A candidate that is not protected, on-request, announce-only, or dry-run is smoked and apply_swap runs on Smoke::Pass. The smoke checks that the plan answered, not that the id is newer.; read-code: The live dry-run rejected grok-4.20 by catalog date, so that id was not on the own list in that run. The own-list path is still in the code. Verify: Unit-test swap_plan with source grok containing grok-4.7 and grok-4.20 and a catalog created stamp that marks 4.20 older; assert it is not a SwapCandidate. Remedy: Apply public_verdict to an own-list id as well when any public source has created stamps for both ids, and do not smoke it when the catalog says it is older.
- **F04-3** [major] `crates/c3/src/maintain/models.rs:320` - public_verdict treats the catalog created integer as proof the candidate is newer. A hostile or compromised catalog body can stamp an older same-family id with a later created value, pass the gate, and be seated after a smoke that only checks that the plan still serves it. Trigger: A catalog JSON object whose id matches the successor rule and whose created value is greater than the seated id's created value, while the plan still answers for that older id. Evidence: read-code: A catalog hit with created c and seated date cs returns Ok when c > cs. The value is serde_json as_i64 from the body, with no other clock.; read-code: The id itself must match valid_model_id, so this cannot break roster JSON or the smoke argv. It can still replace the model string. Verify: Feed a fixture catalog where grok-4.20 has a created stamp later than grok-4.7 and a scripted smoke pass; assert the roster model does not change. Remedy: Do not seat a public id on date order alone when the version pair is the known older-higher pattern, or require the smoke to observe a model identity the old id cannot produce. At minimum, refuse a candidate whose version is higher but whose id is already recorded as older in a previous state.
- **F04-4** [major] `crates/c3/src/cli/doctor.rs:88`, `crates/c3/src/setup/repo_models.rs:251` - c3 doctor --fix rewrites agent pins and AGENTS.md even when C3_CHILD=1. The child guard exists only in hook_line, so a reviewer or worker that runs doctor --fix edits the repository under review and the edit lands in its diff. Trigger: A C3-started claude reviewer or worker, with C3_CHILD=1, runs c3 doctor --fix in the repository. Evidence: read-code: args.fix calls refresh_repo_models with the roster models and no in_c3_child check.; read-code: in_c3_child is consulted only at the start of hook_line. Verify: With C3_CHILD=1, run c3 doctor --fix on a repo whose .claude/agents file pins claude-opus-4-8 and assert the file is unchanged. Remedy: Return before refresh_repo_models when engines::in_c3_child() is true, in doctor --fix and inside refresh_repo_models itself.
- **F04-5** [major] `crates/c3/src/engines/kimi.rs:215`, `crates/c3/src/engines/kimi.rs:240` - Kimi worktree removal ignores unlink failures. After unlink_links_inside, remove() always runs git worktree remove --force and remove_dir_all. A junction or directory symlink that was not classified as is_symlink, or that remove_link could not delete, is left for those deleters. The invariant requires nothing outside the worktree to be removed on any error path. Trigger: A reviewer leaves a junction inside the throwaway worktree (for example node_modules pointing at the main checkout) and unlink fails or does not see it. Evidence: read-code: unlink_links_inside's result is discarded. git worktree remove --force and remove_dir_all always follow.; read-code: Only FileType::is_symlink is unlinked. Other directory entries are pushed on the walk stack.; read-code: The Windows test asserts a successful unlink of one junction. It does not run remove() after a failed unlink.; assumed: This review did not establish whether Git follows a junction that is still present. Verify: On Windows, hold a junction open so remove_dir fails, call the remove path, and check that a sentinel outside the worktree still exists. Remedy: If unlink_links_inside did not remove every reparse point (use the same FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT test as panel/roles.rs), skip git worktree remove and remove_dir_all and leave the directory for a later prune. Do not delete when any link remains.
- **F04-6** [minor] `crates/c3/src/engines/claude_auth.rs:96`, `crates/c3/src/maintain/mod.rs:1750` - Not every process C3 starts gets C3_CHILD=1. The claude auth-status and --version probe clears the environment and does not set it. The detached maintain process is CreateProcessW with a null environment block, so it only inherits a parent that already has the variable. Trigger: A launcher probe or a maintain pass spawned from a user session that does not already have C3_CHILD. Evidence: read-code: probe() calls env_clear and then only the probe env pairs. scrub_host_markers is not called. Callers pass auth status and --version.; read-code: CreateProcessW is called with lpEnvironment null. The command line is the maintain --run pass, not a Claude session.; read-code: Reviewer and worker turns do call scrub_host_markers after env_clear, so those CLIs get C3_CHILD=1. Verify: Log the environment of claude auth status as started by sign_in, and of the detached maintain pid, and check for C3_CHILD. Remedy: Set C3_CHILD=1 on the probe command and in the detached maintain environment block. Document that Claude subagents must inherit it.
- **F04-7** [minor] `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:216`, `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:592` - Branch classification is wrong in two ordinary layouts. If origin/HEAD is unset and both main and develop exist, main is the default even when the repo's real default is develop, so merged and unknown are computed against the wrong branch. A worktree whose directory name starts with c3-kimi-wt- is dropped from the leftover count even when it is the user's. Trigger: A repository with no origin/HEAD, a local main, and develop as the real default; or a worktree directory named c3-kimi-wt-notes. Evidence: read-code: default_branch uses origin/HEAD when that local branch exists, otherwise the first of main and master that exists, otherwise the current branch.; read-code: is_c3_throwaway_worktree is true when the path's file name starts with c3-kimi-wt-. The scan skips those worktrees. Verify: In a repo with branches main and develop, no origin/HEAD, and develop checked out, run c3 branches and read default_branch. Add a worktree whose folder name starts with c3-kimi-wt- and confirm it is absent. Remedy: Prefer init.defaultBranch and the branch HEAD is born from over a hard-coded main. Treat a worktree as throwaway only when its path is under the temp directory and the name matches the prefix plus the uuid pattern.
- **F04-8** [minor] `crates/c3/src/telemetry/classes.rs:344`, `crates/c3/src/maintain/env.rs:213`, `crates/c3/src/maintain/env.rs:263` - Two privacy and fetch bounds are wider than the stated invariants. For vendor class anthropic, any id of the shape claude-(fable|opus|sonnet|haiku)-<digits>[-<digits>] is sent by name even when it is not in the closed list or the published set. Catalog reads stop at HTTP_BODY_CAP (8 MiB), not the 4 MiB BODY_CAP, and the redirect allow-list permits code.kimi.ai to cdn.kimi.ai for every keyless GET, not only the installer. Trigger: A reviewer classified as anthropic (engine claude with no private base_url, or a host under anthropic.com) whose model is a custom id of that shape; or a catalog that redirects or sends a 5 to 8 MiB body. Evidence: read-code: After the closed list misses, class anthropic returns the lowercased id when is_published_claude_shape matches. published_ids is not consulted.; read-code: HTTP_BODY_CAP is 8 * 1024 * 1024. read_capped uses that cap. web.rs BODY_CAP is 4 MiB and is applied only after a successful read.; read-code: redirect_target allows REDIRECT_HOSTS (code.kimi.ai, cdn.kimi.ai) for every follow_redirects GET, including web::keyless_get. Verify: Emit a telemetry model token for engine claude and model claude-opus-9-9 with an empty published set. Fetch a catalog through a 302 from code.kimi.ai to cdn.kimi.ai and confirm it is followed. Remedy: Send a Claude-shaped id only when it is in CLAUDE_MODELS or the published set. Cap the keyless read at BODY_CAP inside http_get when the caller is the catalog fetch. Restrict the kimi CDN pair to the installer URLs.
- **F04-9** [minor] `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:126`, `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:833` - --clear deletes the first line of any description that starts with c3: , including a human note that does not parse as a record. --set, if git config --get fails, treats the description as empty and overwrites it, dropping a foreign note it could not read. Trigger: A branch description whose first line is c3: hello, or a git config --get that exits non-zero while a description is present. Evidence: read-code: is_c3_description is starts_with("c3: "). clear_state removes that first line whenever this is true, without BranchRecord::parse.; read-code: read_description(...).unwrap_or_default() turns a failed read into an empty string, then git config writes the new record over the key. Verify: Set a description to c3: not a record\nkeep me and run c3 branches --clear. Separately, make git config --get fail and run --set; check whether the previous value remains. Remedy: Treat a c3: line as C3's only when BranchRecord::parse succeeds; otherwise leave it. If the read fails, abort --set instead of writing.

